WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.480
Spadario Amade and his sister Daniela, who both worked on safety at the company, and

00:04.480 --> 00:06.600
accused them of plotting a coup.

00:06.600 --> 00:10.800
Altman told them that he had this on good authority from a senior executive, so Daniela

00:10.800 --> 00:14.640
brought in the executive, who denied having said anything of the sort.

00:14.640 --> 00:18.600
Then Altman insisted to all of them, he'd never made the accusation in the first place.

00:18.600 --> 00:22.320
Daniela lost it, and replied, quote, you just said that.

00:22.320 --> 00:26.960
Later, Altman apologized to the executive, saying he'd just wanted Daniela to stop yelling

00:26.960 --> 00:28.880
and said the first name that came to mind.

00:28.880 --> 00:33.520
Altman says he accused them only of political activity, and the rest isn't quite how he

00:33.520 --> 00:34.520
remembers it.

00:34.520 --> 00:38.680
This is just one small example of a pattern of alleged deceptions documented in our new

00:38.680 --> 00:41.480
investigation, which you can read in the New Yorker.

00:41.480 --> 00:46.280
Some senior executives at Microsoft, one of OpenAI's major partners, said, as one put

00:46.280 --> 00:52.480
it, that Altman has, quote, misrepresented, distorted, renegotiated, reneged on agreements.

00:52.480 --> 00:57.600
One recent example, an OpenAI deal with Amazon that Microsoft executives say may conflict

00:57.600 --> 00:59.280
with an exclusivity agreement.

00:59.280 --> 01:03.760
That senior exec added, quote, I think there's a small but real chance he's eventually remembered

01:03.760 --> 01:07.920
as a Bernie Madoff or a Sam Bankman-free level scammer.

01:07.920 --> 01:11.640
Some government officials told us they came to distrust Altman.

01:11.640 --> 01:16.800
In one meeting, he told intelligence officials China had launched an AGI Manhattan Project,

01:16.800 --> 01:20.480
and that the government had to give OpenAI billions to compete.

01:20.480 --> 01:23.160
Pressed for evidence, he said, I've heard things.

01:23.160 --> 01:25.360
He promised to follow up, and never did.

01:25.360 --> 01:29.800
An official concluded, quote, it was just being used as a sales pitch.

01:29.800 --> 01:33.840
Altman says he doesn't recall describing Beijing's efforts exactly that way.

01:33.840 --> 01:36.160
It turns out these complaints go way back.

01:36.160 --> 01:40.880
At looped his first startup, he told colleagues he was a champion ping pong player, according

01:40.880 --> 01:41.880
to one of them.

01:41.880 --> 01:45.380
Before turning out to be one of the worst players in the office, Altman says he was

01:45.380 --> 01:46.540
probably joking.

01:46.540 --> 01:50.960
At Y Combinator, a startup incubator that Altman ran after that, colleagues remembered

01:50.960 --> 01:55.960
YC's founder saying, quote, Sam had been lying to us all the time.

01:55.960 --> 02:00.440
One fellow Y Combinator founder, a programmer named Aaron Schwartz, not long before his

02:00.440 --> 02:05.400
suicide in 2013, had told a friend, quote, Sam can never be trusted.

02:05.400 --> 02:06.800
He is a sociopath.

02:06.800 --> 02:08.400
He would do anything.

02:08.400 --> 02:13.760
At OpenAI, in late 2022, Altman assured the board that features of a model had been approved

02:13.760 --> 02:15.200
by a safety panel.

02:15.200 --> 02:19.800
Board member Helen Toner requested documentation, and found the most controversial ones had

02:19.800 --> 02:21.080
not been approved.

02:21.080 --> 02:26.040
The next year, he told OpenAI's CTO Mira Marathi that a subsequent version of chat

02:26.040 --> 02:30.520
GPT didn't need a safety review according to the company's general counsel.

02:30.520 --> 02:36.360
When she checked, the general counsel said, quote, of confused where Sam got that impression.

02:36.360 --> 02:37.920
The board fired Altman.

02:37.920 --> 02:41.840
When they pressed him to admit that there was a pattern of deception, he replied, according

02:41.840 --> 02:46.200
to people on the call, quote, I can't change my personality.

02:46.200 --> 02:47.920
Read much more in my full investigation.

